  "hero": {
    "tagline": "Waterfalls, living root bridges and the clearest river in India — a few hours from Guwahati.",
    "intro": [
      "Meghalaya is a high green plateau where the clouds sit low enough to walk through. Shillong is the easy-going capital, Cherrapunji is where the rain makes waterfalls on every cliff, and down at Dawki the Umngot river runs so clear the boats seem to float on air.",
      "Most visitors come for two or three days, but the state rewards a slower trip. Khasi villages grow bridges out of living tree roots, the Jaintia hills hide monoliths and quiet lakes, and the caves around Mawsynram run deeper than most people ever go.",
      "Every tour below is run by our own local team — private car, a driver who knows the roads, and stays we have checked ourselves. Pick a tour, or tell us what you have in mind and we will plan it around you."
    ],
