  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "How many days are enough for a Meghalaya trip?",
      "answer": "Three days covers Shillong, Cherrapunji and Dawki at a comfortable pace. With five or six days you can add the root bridge trek, Mawlynnong and a night camping by the river."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the best time to visit Meghalaya?",
      "answer": "October to April for clear skies and easy travel. June to August if you want the waterfalls at full power and don't mind rain."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do your tours start from Guwahati?",
      "answer": "Yes. Most tours include pickup from Guwahati airport or railway station. Tours that start in Shillong say so on the tour page."
    },
    {
      "question": "Are the tours private?",
      "answer": "Yes. You get your own car and driver-guide; we don't put you in a shared group unless a tour says it is a group departure."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do I need to pay when I book?",
      "answer": "No. Send a booking request and we confirm availability and the final price first. You pay only after you're happy with the plan."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can you change a tour to suit us?",
      "answer": "Yes. Tell us your dates, pace and budget and we'll adjust the route, stays or number of days."
    }
  ],
